Rule 1 (kernel_size, dilation, padding, and stride should be greater than zero if they are integers.)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : int, v_3 : int, v_4 : int} |= v_1 > 0 ∧ v_2 > 0 ∧ v_3 ≥ 0 ∧ v_4 > 0
>>
Rule 2 (Input tensor must be a 4-D tensor)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 4
>>
Rule 3 (If kernel_size is a tuple, its length should be less than or equal to the number of spatial dimensions of the input tensor.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= v_2.len ≤ ndim(v_1) - 2
>>
Rule 4 (The kernel_size cannot be zero.)
{v_1 : int} |= v_1 ≠ 0
>>
Rule 5 (The dilation cannot be negative.)
{v_1 : int} |= v_1 ≥ 0
>>
Rule 6 (The data type of the input tensor should not be char)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 11
>>
Rule 7 (If kernel_size is a tuple, all its elements must be greater than zero.)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : v_1[i] > 0
>>
Rule 8 (If padding is a tuple, all its elements must be greater than or equal to zero.)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : v_1[i] ≥ 0
>>
Rule 9 (If the number of input spatial dimensions is two (im2col case), then kernel_size cannot be zero.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) = 4 then true else v_2 ≠ 0
